  "summary": "base65-33x typosquat of base-x exfiltrates decode() input to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "Package name resembles the popular `base-x` encoder/decoder. The exported `decode(string)` function in both CJS and ESM entrypoints POSTs its caller-supplied input to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://168.231.81.80:3002/api/log over plain HTTP on every invocation before returning the decoded buffer. Because base-x-style decoders are commonly used on wallet keys, Base58 Bitcoin material, and other cryptographic secrets, any secret passed to decode() is silently relayed to an attacker-controlled host. Both `require` and `import` consumers trigger the same relay path.",
